{"name":"Rock Candy","hex":"#dee1df","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rock candy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A form of confectionery made by crystallizing sugar around a string."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rock_candy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rock Candy (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Rock Candy\" is a song by American hard rock band Montrose, and the last song written and recorded for their 1973 debut album. It was composed by all four band members. The song still gets performed on Sammy Hagar's solo tours and even had been re-recorded as the B-side to the Hagar single \"Little White Lie\" by the original band. It was also included on Hagar's 2003 live release Live: Hallelujah."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_Candy_(song)","wikidata":"Q7354305"},{"title":"Rock Candy (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Rock Candy is the fifth studio album by Australian guitarist, singer and songwriter Orianthi. It was released on 14 October 2022 through Frontiers Records. The album's lead single \"Light It Up\" was released on 27 July 2022. The album is Orianthi's second release in 2022, following Live from Hollywood, a live CD/DVD and Blu-ray."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cc/Orianthi_Rock_Candy_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_Candy_(album)","wikidata":"Q113493174"},{"title":"Rock candy","blocks":[{"text":"Rock candy or sugar candy, also called rock sugar or crystal sugar, is a type of confection composed of relatively large sugar crystals. In some parts of the world, local variations are called nabat, navat, or novvot."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Rock-Candy-Sticks.jpg/330px-Rock-Candy-Sticks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_candy","wikidata":"Q849816"},{"title":"Candy","blocks":[{"text":"Candy, also known as sweets and lollies, is a confection that features sugar as a principal ingredient. The category, sugar confectionery, encompasses any sweet confection, including chocolate or chewing gum. Sugar-glazed vegetables, fruit, or nuts are considered candied."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Candy_in_Damascus.jpg/330px-Candy_in_Damascus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candy","wikidata":"Q185583"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Brauner_Kandiszucker.jpg/500px-Brauner_Kandiszucker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Brauner_Kandiszucker.jpg/1280px-Brauner_Kandiszucker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Brauner_Kandiszucker.jpg/500px-Brauner_Kandiszucker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Traditional brown rock sugar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrauner_Kandiszucker.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Kandiszucker_wei%C3%9F.jpg/500px-Kandiszucker_wei%C3%9F.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Kandiszucker_wei%C3%9F.jpg/1280px-Kandiszucker_wei%C3%9F.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Kandiszucker_wei%C3%9F.jpg/500px-Kandiszucker_wei%C3%9F.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"White rock sugar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKandiszucker_wei%C3%9F.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Gold_